  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Beav Creator",
      "text": "Beav Creator brings Xiaohongshu (RED/RedNote), social-media operations, and creator AI workflows into DeepSeek Harness. Use it for topic and trend research, knowledge management, copywriting, cover and post images, audio, short video, and durable multi-step content production. It exposes Beav workspaces, projects, tasks, approvals, and verified artifacts through Cordis services, Harness tools, background jobs, slash commands, session events, and Web client contributions. It does not use MCP."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requirements:\n\n- Beav 2.7.4 or later\n- DeepSeek Harness `0.1.0-rc.6` or later (`rc.7` / `rc.8` web clients require `beav-creator-dsh@0.1.5` or later)\n- Node.js 22 or later\n\nInstall into a Harness profile:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add beav-creator-dsh\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Start that profile, open **Settings → Plugins → Beav Creator**, and select **Connect Beav**. Harness opens `beav://connect/authorize`; Beav starts if needed and shows the requested permissions. After you approve in Beav, the connector completes a five-minute, single-use PKCE exchange and stores the resulting credential under `BEAV_CREATOR_TOKEN`. No token is copied through the clipboard, URL, browser client, chat, session event, or tool result."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "If Beav is not running, an operation that needs it opens `beav://open` once and performs a bounded health retry. You can override the local endpoint or credential reference in the profile patch:\n\n```yaml\n- update:\n    id: beav\n    config:\n      endpoint: http://127.0.0.1:41700\n\nOnly loopback HTTP endpoints are accepted."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "- Ask naturally: “Use Beav to research a Xiaohongshu topic and turn the latest knowledge in my launch workspace into a post, cover images, and a 60-second video.”\n- Type `@beav` to select a stable workspace or project reference.\n- Use `/beav connect`, `/beav status`, `/beav open`, `/beav workspaces`, `/beav new`, `/beav import`, or `/beav save` for direct actions without a model turn.\n- Long-running work appears as a native Harness job and a replayable Beav task card.\n- Completion is accepted only after Beav reports durable artifact read-back verification and each returned artifact can be read back through the Creator Gateway."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "Beav retains ownership of AI orchestration, knowledge access, media generation, approvals, billing, persistence, and artifact verification. The connector cannot auto-approve paid or destructive actions."
    },
    {
      "section": "Trust and privacy",
      "text": "This package runs as trusted local Host code. Pairing exposes only a local approval/status surface before authorization; creator operations still require a revocable client credential. Deep links contain a random request ID and PKCE challenge, never a token or verifier. The connector connects only to Beav on loopback, requests bounded summaries, and never transfers raw media bytes through model tool parameters. The connector source is public so the community can audit the integration. The Beav desktop application, creator runtime, knowledge engine, media pipeline, and commercial services remain proprietary and are not included in this repository or npm package."
    },
    {
      "section": "Trust and privacy",
      "text": "This is a community plugin and is not an official DeepSeek product or endorsement."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Clone the official Harness checkout at the pinned compatibility revision beside this repository:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness.git ../deepseek-harness\ngit -C ../deepseek-harness checkout 47f943859bef60e4160492346772ded9b24f765a\npnpm -C ../deepseek-harness install\npnpm -C ../deepseek-harness run build:lib"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "The published tarball contains prebuilt `lib/` files and treats every Harness runtime package as a peer dependency. Users do not run a build or prepare script during plugin installation."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT. This license applies to the connector only, not to the Beav application or services."
    }
